# Frontend

- Components live in `frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx`.
- Pages live in `frontend/src/pages/[PageName].page.tsx` and set `document.title`. `main.tsx` picks the page from `location.hash`: no hash is the browser UI, `#/popup/<kind>` is a popup, `#/<page>` is a `ce://` page.
- Every HTML element gets an `id` as its first attribute.
- Style with Tailwind. Merge classes with `cn()` from `frontend/src/lib/cn.ts`.
- The browser UI view sits behind the page views. Menus or panels that would overlap the page open through `openPopup` instead of rendering in place.

```tsx
export function DownloadsPage() {
  useEffect(() => {
    document.title = "Downloads";
  }, []);

  return <main id="downloads-page">...</main>;
}
```

A new IPC call needs three pieces: a Rust command, a camelCase type in `types/browser.ts`, and a wrapper in `frontend/src/lib/browser-client.ts`.
